---
import CodeBlock from './CodeBlock.astro';
const selfAlias = 'robertGPT';
---
<div class="experience" data-experience>
  <div class="study-toolbar"><span class="study-label">VOX / APP STUDY</span><div class="view-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Explore the Vox app concept" data-view-tabs hidden><button id="tab-room" role="tab" aria-selected="true" aria-controls="view-room" data-view="room" tabindex="0">Room</button><button id="tab-keyring" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="view-keyring" data-view="keyring" tabindex="-1">Keyring</button><button id="tab-services" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="view-services" data-view="services" tabindex="-1">Services</button></div><span class="study-hint">TRY THE VIEWS ↗</span></div>
  <div class="app-window">
    <aside class="app-sidebar" aria-label="Illustrative rooms and acting identity">
      <div class="app-identity"><span class="identity-facet" aria-hidden="true">◈</span><div><strong>{selfAlias}</strong><span><i class="live-dot" aria-hidden="true"></i> node attached</span></div></div>
      <p class="app-label">ROOMS <span>4</span></p>
      <ul class="room-list"><li class="selected-room"><span>family</span><span class="room-unread" aria-label="1 unread message">1</span></li><li><span>build-vox</span></li><li><span>taxes-2026</span></li><li><span>weekend</span></li></ul>
      <div class="sidebar-bottom"><span class="app-label">ON THIS MACHINE</span><p>{selfAlias} <span>attached</span></p><p>claude-mbp <span>attached</span></p><small>Separate identities.<br />One daemon.</small></div>
    </aside>
    <div class="app-workspace">
      <section id="view-room" class="app-view room-view" aria-labelledby="room-heading" data-panel="room">
        <div class="room-main"><header class="app-view-header"><div><p class="app-label">ROOM</p><h3 id="room-heading">family</h3></div><span class="app-meta">5 members · retention forever</span></header>
          <div class="timeline"><div class="day-divider"><span>Sunday, October 4</span></div>
            <article class="chat-row"><time>18:02</time><div><h4>ann <span aria-label="mutual trust">⇄</span></h4><p>The photos are on the NAS. SSH is shared here if you need it.</p></div></article>
            <article class="chat-row"><time>18:04</time><div><h4>nas <span aria-label="mutual trust">⇄</span></h4><div class="inline-service"><div><span class="service-symbol" aria-hidden="true">↗</span><div><strong>nas-ssh</strong><code>nas-ssh.nas.family.vox</code></div></div><button type="button" class="inline-action" data-open-view="services" hidden>Open services <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></button></div></div></article>
            <article class="chat-row own-message"><time>18:07</time><div><h4>you <span>as {selfAlias}</span></h4><p>Perfect. See you both at seven.</p></div></article>
            <div class="day-divider unread-divider"><span>1 unread</span></div>
            <article class="chat-row"><time>18:11</time><div><h4>bea <span aria-label="mutual trust">⇄</span></h4><p>I’ll bring dessert.</p><div class="file-offer"><span aria-hidden="true">▤</span><div><strong>recipe.pdf</strong><span>220 KB · file offered by bea</span></div><span class="file-state">Not fetched</span></div></div></article>
          </div>
          <div class="composer-study"><span>{selfAlias} <span aria-hidden="true">▸</span></span><p>Message family…</p><span class="composer-label">PREVIEW</span></div>
        </div>
        <aside class="room-inspector" aria-label="Room members and trust"><p class="app-label">MEMBERS <span>YOU + 4</span></p><ul class="member-list"><li><span class="trust-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⇄</span><div><strong>ann</strong><p>In your keyring</p><small>You can read each other</small></div></li><li><span class="trust-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⇄</span><div><strong>bea</strong><p>In your keyring</p><small>You can read each other</small></div></li><li><span class="trust-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⇄</span><div><strong>nas</strong><p>In your keyring</p><small>You can read each other</small></div></li><li class="unknown-member"><span class="trust-glyph" aria-hidden="true">·</span><div><strong>K2M9·Q7RT</strong><p>Not in your keyring</p><small>Compare the full fingerprint</small></div></li></ul><button type="button" class="inspector-link" data-open-view="keyring" hidden>Explore your keyring <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></button><div class="inspector-note"><span class="app-label">YOUR ALIASES</span><p>These names are yours.<br />Nobody else can name a node for you.</p></div></aside>
      </section>
      <section id="view-keyring" class="app-view detail-view" aria-labelledby="keyring-heading" data-panel="keyring" hidden>
        <header class="app-view-header"><div><p class="app-label">{selfAlias}’S KEYRING</p><h3 id="keyring-heading">Trust has a direction.</h3></div><span class="app-meta">3 trusted nodes</span></header>
        <div class="keyring-layout"><div class="keyring-entries"><div class="keyring-entry"><span class="trust-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⇄</span><strong>ann</strong><span>Your alias</span></div><div class="keyring-entry"><span class="trust-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⇄</span><strong>bea</strong><span>Your alias</span></div><div class="keyring-entry"><span class="trust-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⇄</span><strong>nas</strong><span>Your alias</span></div><p>Not a contact directory.<br />Only the nodes you chose to trust.</p></div><div class="keyring-card"><span class="app-label">UNDERSTANDING ANN’S ACCESS</span><h4>ann <span aria-hidden="true">⇄</span> {selfAlias}</h4><div class="trust-direction"><strong>{selfAlias} → ann</strong><p>You trust Ann. Your node releases your sender keys to Ann in shared rooms.</p></div><div class="trust-direction"><strong>ann → {selfAlias}</strong><p>Ann trusts you too. Each node accepts the other’s keys. You can read each other.</p></div><div class="scope-note"><strong>Shared rooms: family · taxes-2026</strong><p>Trust also covers services you share in these rooms—and any rooms you share later.</p></div><details class="trust-detail"><summary>What would removing Ann change?</summary><p>Future sender keys rotate. Ann loses access to your shared services, including live sessions. You stop accepting Ann’s keys. What Ann already read or copied cannot be taken back.</p><p>This study does not change a real keyring.</p></details></div></div>
      </section>
      <section id="view-services" class="app-view detail-view" aria-labelledby="services-heading" data-panel="services" hidden>
        <header class="app-view-header"><div><p class="app-label">FAMILY / SERVICES</p><h3 id="services-heading">An address in your own names.</h3></div><span class="app-meta">Shared by nas</span></header>
        <div class="service-study"><div class="service-summary"><span class="service-symbol" aria-hidden="true">↗</span><div><h4>nas-ssh <span>TCP</span></h4><p>Shared in family · nas trusts you</p></div><span class="service-live"><i class="live-dot" aria-hidden="true"></i> online · example</span></div><CodeBlock code={`ssh ${selfAlias}@nas-ssh.nas.family.vox`} label="Example SSH command" /><div class="service-needs"><span>✓ proxy configured</span><span>✓ node attached</span><span>✓ nas trusts you</span><span>✓ nas online</span></div><div class="address-anatomy" aria-label="Address structure"><div><code>nas-ssh</code><span>service</span></div><b aria-hidden="true">.</b><div><code>nas</code><span>your node alias</span></div><b aria-hidden="true">.</b><div><code>family</code><span>your room alias</span></div><b aria-hidden="true">.</b><div><code>vox</code><span>Vox address</span></div></div><p class="service-explanation">No public link. No separate permission matrix. The host’s keyring and your shared room determine access.</p><details class="trust-detail"><summary>When something is missing</summary><p>If the host is offline, the service is unavailable. If trust is withdrawn, access ends and live sessions are cut. A copy box should name the missing condition—not hide it behind “connection failed.”</p></details><p class="example-warning">Illustrative command and readiness states. This website is not connected to a Vox daemon; copying does not create or test a connection.</p></div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="app-status"><span><i class="live-dot" aria-hidden="true"></i> {selfAlias} · attached <span class="status-separator">/</span> connected to 3 peers</span><span>keyring open 23m · example state</span></div>
  <noscript><p class="no-script-note">This is an illustrative room view. Enable JavaScript to explore the proposed keyring and service views. No real keys or messages are used.</p></noscript>
</div>
<script src="../scripts/experience.ts"></script>
